So guess who believed him in his lifetime?

263
00:13:16.280 --> 00:13:21.560
So we're like that somebody put it to me one day.

264
00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:24.360
When I want something I wanted yesterday,

265
00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:28.400
we don't want to wait and we don't want to have any patience.

266
00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:33.400
So we don't realize that as far as the Lord is concerned,

267
00:13:33.400 --> 00:13:38.460
we only have a few minutes to live if that.

268
00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:43.020
Because a thousand years is like a single day in God's eyes.

269
00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:46.400
And so, as far as he's concerned,

270
00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:50.560
the purification he's doing within us is minimal.

271
00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:54.200
And it's in a very short space of time.

272
00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:55.240
But we don't see it that way

273
00:13:55.240 --> 00:13:58.160
because we are in a different dimension.

274
00:13:58.160 --> 00:13:59.400
Okay.

275
00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:02.000
So August the 3rd, 1910,

276
00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:03.920
we're talking about voluntary sin,

277
00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:08.000
no possibility of divine will with voluntary sin.

278
00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:09.400
Now, voluntary sin,

279
00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:11.600
I always illustrate it on the person on my right,

280
00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:13.160
if you excuse me.

281
00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:17.280
Voluntary sin is I want to get my own back on you.

282
00:14:17.280 --> 00:14:18.920
Notice the I want.

283
00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:21.360
I want to give you a piece of my mind.

284
00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:26.080
I want to bring you down a peg.

285
00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:28.680
I'm using all expressions that are used in Ireland.

286
00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:29.520
Okay.

287
00:14:29.520 --> 00:14:32.880
And that's voluntary sin against love.

288
00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:37.000
And it's also different forms of revenge.

289
00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:41.360
So it's actually very serious if it's voluntary.

290
00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:44.320
It's a different subject when it's involuntary.

291
00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:46.960
'Cause you can always say, sorry, I didn't mean to say that.

292
00:14:46.960 --> 00:14:48.560
And you can say it truthfully.

293
00:14:48.560 --> 00:14:49.400
Do you know what I mean?

294
00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:50.720
If it's involuntary.

295
00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:53.360
So the Lord doesn't treat involuntary sin

296
00:14:53.360 --> 00:14:55.240
the same way as he does with voluntary.

297
00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:58.160
So Louisa said,

298
00:14:58.160 --> 00:14:59.680
"As I was in my usual state,

299
00:14:59.680 --> 00:15:03.040
"Blessed Jesus came for just a little and told me,

300
00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:06.760
"listen my daughter, miseries and weaknesses,

301
00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:09.200
"our means in order to find oneself

302
00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:10.920
"in the harbor of divinity."

303
00:15:10.920 --> 00:15:13.160
Now miseries and weaknesses are the struggles

304
00:15:13.160 --> 00:15:14.480
we have with ourself.

305
00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:21.760
And the Lord says, "Your struggles are not a problem.

306
00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:24.720
"Only voluntary sin is a problem."

307
00:15:24.720 --> 00:15:27.440
If we get that very clear in our heads

308
00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:31.640
because many people, when they go to confession,

309
00:15:31.640 --> 00:15:33.360
good people I'm talking about,

310
00:15:33.360 --> 00:15:34.960
actually confess a struggle.

311
00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:36.820
They don't actually confess sin.

312
00:15:37.960 --> 00:15:42.960
And they very often are not actually giving enough material

313
00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:45.640
for the sacrament to be operative.

314
00:15:45.640 --> 00:15:47.080
So the priest will say,

315
00:15:47.080 --> 00:15:48.960
could you mention something in your past life

316
00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:50.240
that you're sorry for?

317
00:15:50.240 --> 00:15:52.080
And it's not that it wasn't forgiven,

318
00:15:52.080 --> 00:15:54.880
but it's only that that will be the material

319
00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:57.560
that's needed for this particular sacrament.

320
00:15:57.560 --> 00:15:59.480
We don't realize that.

321
00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:02.040
So we need to be very clear that struggle

322
00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:05.840
and temptation are not matters for confession.

323
00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:07.340
They are for spiritual direction

324
00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:08.720
which is a different subject.

325
00:16:08.720 --> 00:16:12.320
But voluntary sin, yes.

326
00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:14.120
Even involuntary sin, yes.

327
00:16:14.120 --> 00:16:18.720
So the Lord says, "The miseries and the weaknesses

328
00:16:18.720 --> 00:16:20.760
"are means in order to find oneself

329
00:16:20.760 --> 00:16:21.920
"in the harbor of divinity."

330
00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:24.680
That means the more you conquer them,

331
00:16:24.680 --> 00:16:28.480
the more room you make for the divine will to come and reign

332
00:16:28.480 --> 00:16:31.840
in you and for the kingdom of God to be in you.

333
00:16:34.400 --> 00:16:39.400
I think it's two Corinthians 5, 17.

334
00:16:39.400 --> 00:16:43.720
It won't go out of my head so I have to write it down.

335
00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:48.720
Think it's that we are to reign in life with Christ.

336
00:16:48.720 --> 00:16:51.200
Okay, and you can only reign in life

337
00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:54.640
as you hand over more and more and more bits of yourself

338
00:16:54.640 --> 00:16:56.600
to him so that he can take over.

339
00:16:56.600 --> 00:16:59.880
So reigning in life means that you're actually living

340
00:16:59.880 --> 00:17:03.520
all your thoughts, words, actions, movement, steps

341
00:17:03.520 --> 00:17:07.840
to use Louisa's words, you're actually living all of that

342
00:17:07.840 --> 00:17:10.000
out of love, not out of anything else.

343
00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:15.600
So because in feeling the burden of human miseries,

344
00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:17.400
that's the struggles we have.

345
00:17:17.400 --> 00:17:19.240
The soul gets annoyed, gets bothered,

346
00:17:19.240 --> 00:17:21.680
and tries to get rid of her self.

347
00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:24.320
Now I put self in inverted commas

348
00:17:24.320 --> 00:17:26.440
'cause you can't get rid of yourself.

349
00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:28.240
If you get rid of yourself, you're dead.

350
00:17:28.240 --> 00:17:31.880
The translator should have said, "You're ego."

351
00:17:33.120 --> 00:17:36.200
So it's actually better, I just put inverted commas there

352
00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:41.200
and write ego in the margin there to remind you.

353
00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:47.040
So getting rid of her ego, she already finds herself in God.

354
00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:50.360
That means you put your all your selfishness aside

355
00:17:50.360 --> 00:17:52.160
and divine love takes over.

356
00:17:52.160 --> 00:17:53.680
That's the way it is.

357
00:17:53.680 --> 00:17:56.840
Then having placed my arm around Jesus' neck, Louisa,

358
00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:59.880
said he'd clung against my face and then disappeared.

359
00:18:00.880 --> 00:18:04.280
Later as he came back and I was lamenting

360
00:18:04.280 --> 00:18:07.120
for he had run away like a flash without giving me time,

361
00:18:07.120 --> 00:18:10.360
that is giving her time as an Italian to do a bit of talking.

362
00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:13.920
Okay, and that's a tragedy initially

363
00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:16.320
if you don't give them time to egg the tongue.

364
00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:19.280
Jesus told me, "Since it displeases you,

365
00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:22.320
"take me, bind me, as you want,

366
00:18:22.320 --> 00:18:24.360
"and don't let me run away."

367
00:18:24.360 --> 00:18:27.920
So Louisa said, "Bravo, Jesus,

368
00:18:27.920 --> 00:18:30.120
"what a beautiful proposal you make me,

369
00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:33.200
"but then can this be done with you?

370
00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:37.040
"You let yourself be bound and last as much as one can,

371
00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:40.280
"but at the best moment, she said, you disappear,

372
00:18:40.280 --> 00:18:42.400
"and you no longer let yourself be found."

373
00:18:42.400 --> 00:18:46.040
So she's letting him know that I mean you and being can't do this.

374
00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:49.000
It's like a child putting their hand out

375
00:18:49.000 --> 00:18:52.320
to try and see can they capture the sunbeam, you know?

376
00:18:52.320 --> 00:18:54.960
And then they put the hand, the sunbeam is still there,

377
00:18:54.960 --> 00:18:56.360
they can't get it.

378
00:18:56.360 --> 00:18:59.120
And that's what she's saying to him.

379
00:18:59.120 --> 00:19:01.880
"Bravo, Jesus, she said, you're trying to make fun of me,

380
00:19:01.880 --> 00:19:03.920
"but after all, do whatever you want.

381
00:19:03.920 --> 00:19:08.360
"What I care is that you tell me where I offend you,

382
00:19:08.360 --> 00:19:10.560
"and in what I displeased you,

383
00:19:10.560 --> 00:19:12.320
"because you no longer come as before.

384
00:19:12.320 --> 00:19:14.920
"Do you notice she doesn't take the message?

385
00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:16.560
"There's one message she won't take,

386
00:19:16.560 --> 00:19:19.200
"and that is, he's staying away for chastisements,

387
00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:21.280
"not because she has sinned.

388
00:19:21.280 --> 00:19:23.360
"Because if she has sinned, she's not in divine."

389
00:19:23.360 --> 00:19:25.560
Well, it's actually that simple.

390
00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:28.320
It's fascinating for me to see that area

391
00:19:28.320 --> 00:19:30.000
of blindness in her,

392
00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:31.760
'cause we all have blind areas.

393
00:19:31.760 --> 00:19:33.480
We don't think we have what other people

394
00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:35.140
can see them quite clearly.

395
00:19:35.140 --> 00:19:39.000
'Cause we all, we even say of one another,

396
00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:41.680
"You can't tell him that, you're near it."

397
00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:45.400
And still point saying that to her.

398
00:19:45.400 --> 00:19:48.840
'Cause we have areas where we switch on the deaf ear.

399
00:19:48.840 --> 00:19:51.400
We don't listen, it's deliberate,

400
00:19:51.400 --> 00:19:53.760
and it's actually quite important for us to wake up

401
00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:57.320
and realize, what is it that I don't want to listen to?

402
00:19:57.320 --> 00:20:00.080
'Cause it'll always be something challenging, you know?

403
00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:05.080
So, Jesus said, "My daughter do not trouble yourself

404
00:20:05.080 --> 00:20:08.880
"when there is true sin that is voluntary sin."

405
00:20:08.880 --> 00:20:12.240
It's not necessary for me to say it,

406
00:20:12.240 --> 00:20:15.120
the soul already perceives it by herself.

407
00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:17.320
Because, this is very interesting.

408
00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:21.880
When sin is voluntary, it upsets the natural humors.

409
00:20:21.880 --> 00:20:23.520
Now, I looked up the dictionaries

410
00:20:23.520 --> 00:20:25.880
and they don't have the word humor anymore.

411
00:20:25.880 --> 00:20:27.200
It's an ancient word.

412
00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:33.120
So, the way I put it is, you get into bad form.

413
00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:34.680
You know, you get out of sorts

414
00:20:34.680 --> 00:20:36.840
is the way we would put it.

415
00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:40.560
Or to put it very simply, we say, "You get upset."

416
00:20:40.560 --> 00:20:42.200
Okay, so that's what he's saying.

417
00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:46.480
That when sin is voluntary,

418
00:20:46.480 --> 00:20:47.400
you know it immediately,

419
00:20:47.400 --> 00:20:49.200
your conscience isn't dead for him and say,

420
00:20:49.200 --> 00:20:50.720
"And you get upset."

421
00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:54.520
And then man undergoes as though a transformation in evil,

422
00:20:54.520 --> 00:20:56.360
that is if they persist in it.

423
00:20:56.360 --> 00:20:59.800
He feels as though soaked with the sin

424
00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:02.800
he has voluntarily committed.

425
00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:06.040
You know, it's a voluntary that we're underlining.

426
00:21:06.040 --> 00:21:10.440
Just as true virtue transforms the soul into good,

427
00:21:10.440 --> 00:21:14.320
her humors remain all in harmony among themselves.

428
00:21:14.320 --> 00:21:17.240
In other words, all your emotions remain balanced.

429
00:21:17.240 --> 00:21:19.640
So, I think humors is probably emotions.

430
00:21:19.640 --> 00:21:23.280
All in harmony among themselves

431
00:21:23.280 --> 00:21:25.720
and her nature feels as though soaked with sweetness,

432
00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:28.640
with charity, that is with divine love

433
00:21:28.640 --> 00:21:32.040
and with peace, so it is with sin.

434
00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:34.600
So, have you perceived this turmoil?

435
00:21:34.600 --> 00:21:37.200
Have you felt as though soaked within patience,

436
00:21:37.200 --> 00:21:39.240
with anger or with disturbances?

437
00:21:39.240 --> 00:21:41.360
Now, what he's done there is he's given us

438
00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:44.840
a very important piece of discernment.

439
00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:47.560
And if you're helping somebody else,

440
00:21:47.560 --> 00:21:49.760
have you ever heard somebody say to you,

441
00:21:49.760 --> 00:21:51.600
"I should have no peace of mind."

442
00:21:52.760 --> 00:21:55.040
Yeah, there's sin in the life.

443
00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:56.680
You can't have peace of mind.

444
00:21:56.680 --> 00:21:57.840
That's the disturbance.

445
00:21:57.840 --> 00:22:03.960
And so, when you have this information,

446
00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:08.120
it means that you can reach out and help another person.

447
00:22:08.120 --> 00:22:11.440
I remember being in a church all by myself

448
00:22:11.440 --> 00:22:13.760
and somewhere in London.

449
00:22:13.760 --> 00:22:16.480
And I love praying in a church in an afternoon

450
00:22:16.480 --> 00:22:18.640
where you're fairly sure nobody's going to come in.

451
00:22:18.640 --> 00:22:22.640
When a lady did come in and she pushed in beside me

452
00:22:23.600 --> 00:22:25.760
and the church was empty, yeah.

453
00:22:25.760 --> 00:22:28.760
So, I actually had a turn to her and say,

454
00:22:28.760 --> 00:22:30.560
"What can I do for you?"

455
00:22:30.560 --> 00:22:33.840
And she said, "Where did you get your peace from?"

456
00:22:33.840 --> 00:22:35.760
She said, "I felt it outside the door."

457
00:22:35.760 --> 00:22:39.480
Now, if she felt my peace outside the door,

458
00:22:39.480 --> 00:22:41.960
that meant she was very troubled.

459
00:22:41.960 --> 00:22:45.160
And I said, "How did you know there was anybody in here?"

460
00:22:45.160 --> 00:22:46.440
She said, "I don't know."

461
00:22:46.440 --> 00:22:48.120
She said, "It was like as if a voice said,

462
00:22:48.120 --> 00:22:50.560
"Go in there, somebody will help you."

463
00:22:50.560 --> 00:22:53.160
I said, "Oh, you're a guardian angel that's working overtime."

464
00:22:53.160 --> 00:22:58.120
And so, when she said, "Where did you get your peace from?"

465
00:22:58.120 --> 00:23:00.760
And I said, "How much would you pay for something

466
00:23:00.760 --> 00:23:03.240
"absolutely, absolutely divine?"

467
00:23:03.240 --> 00:23:04.960
Or she said, "Anything."

468
00:23:04.960 --> 00:23:07.800
I said, "Well, I'll tell you then."

469
00:23:07.800 --> 00:23:10.800
It was not cheap because you have to deal

470
00:23:10.800 --> 00:23:12.360
with whatever is disturbing you.

471
00:23:12.360 --> 00:23:15.640
And it was amazing.

472
00:23:15.640 --> 00:23:19.200
And it was just something that the Lord took over,

473
00:23:19.200 --> 00:23:20.560
do you know what I mean?

474
00:23:20.560 --> 00:23:22.360
I was able to send her into confession.

475
00:23:22.360 --> 00:23:24.640
I said, "Go in there and get your peace now."

476
00:23:24.640 --> 00:23:26.640
'Cause I knew there was a priest in there.

477
00:23:26.640 --> 00:23:32.800
And everything was, it was one of those divine moments

478
00:23:32.800 --> 00:23:37.000
where you knew it was her time for grace, do you know what I mean?

479
00:23:37.000 --> 00:23:39.480
But this kind of information can really help you

480
00:23:39.480 --> 00:23:40.720
to help somebody else.

481
00:23:40.720 --> 00:23:47.080
So notice the impatience, the anger and the disturbance.

482
00:23:47.080 --> 00:23:50.080
In other words, the soul is out of sorts.

483
00:23:50.080 --> 00:23:56.200
And while he was saying this, he seemed to look deep into me

484
00:23:56.200 --> 00:23:57.920
to see whether it was in me or not.

485
00:23:57.920 --> 00:24:00.880
Do you remember he looked steadily at the rich young man?

486
00:24:00.880 --> 00:24:03.280
He's kind of penetrating you.

487
00:24:03.280 --> 00:24:05.120
And it seemed there wasn't anything there.

488
00:24:05.120 --> 00:24:08.800
And he said, "So yourself have seen," as he said.

489
00:24:08.800 --> 00:24:12.280
So I want to give you the book of Syrach, chapter 40.

490
00:24:12.280 --> 00:24:17.040
Syrach, S-I-R, is Ecclesiasticus.

491
00:24:17.040 --> 00:24:19.560
Chapter 40, verses one to 11.

492
00:24:19.560 --> 00:24:24.160
I don't say Ecclesiasticus because there's two books

493
00:24:24.160 --> 00:24:29.000
almost identical in name Ecclesiastes and Ecclesiasticus.

494
00:24:29.000 --> 00:24:34.120
And those names are given because of ancient translations.

495
00:24:34.120 --> 00:24:37.280
The Ecclesiastes was written by Kovalet

496
00:24:37.280 --> 00:24:39.520
and the other one was written by Syrach.

497
00:24:39.520 --> 00:24:41.960
So we now refer it just to Syrach and Kovalet.

498
00:24:41.960 --> 00:24:44.000
And then you know, you're dealing with two completely

499
00:24:44.000 --> 00:24:45.760
different books, okay.

500
00:24:47.680 --> 00:24:49.520
So Louisa said, "I don't know why."

501
00:24:49.520 --> 00:24:50.720
But while he was saying this,

502
00:24:50.720 --> 00:24:52.840
he showed more earthquakes and destruction

503
00:24:52.840 --> 00:24:55.600
of entire cities, revolutions and many other troubles

504
00:24:55.600 --> 00:24:56.480
and then disappeared.

505
00:24:56.480 --> 00:25:00.520
That was to keep her on track for a reparation, okay.

506
00:25:00.520 --> 00:25:04.160
So August the 12th, 1910,

507
00:25:04.160 --> 00:25:09.000
the origin of all the evil in priests

508
00:25:09.000 --> 00:25:12.120
is in dealing with souls about human things.

509
00:25:12.120 --> 00:25:14.400
Now let me translate that for you.

510
00:25:14.400 --> 00:25:17.000
The origin of evil in priests he says

511
00:25:17.000 --> 00:25:19.280
is dealing on the wrong level.

512
00:25:19.280 --> 00:25:22.760
If you only deal with them on the human level,

513
00:25:22.760 --> 00:25:25.720
you'll never be able to raise them to the divine.

514
00:25:25.720 --> 00:25:27.520
That is the mistake that's been made

515
00:25:27.520 --> 00:25:30.120
in the last 60 or 70 years,

516
00:25:30.120 --> 00:25:32.480
that they've gone over to psychology

517
00:25:32.480 --> 00:25:36.080
and all of this psychoanalysts and all the rest of it.

518
00:25:36.080 --> 00:25:38.880
